{"id":"xminicom.1","n":"xminicom","s":"1","src":{"r":{"pkg":"minicom","ver":"2.7.1-17.el9","repo":"BaseOS","url":"https://dl.rockylinux.org/vault/rocky/9.6/BaseOS/x86_64/os/Packages/m/minicom-2.7.1-17.el9.x86_64.rpm","path":"/usr/share/man/man1/xminicom.1.gz","sha256":"5d56f6e0239918ca6dffa25c7d74b9b47e990d03d3786544d58a37ce6175ddd0","date":"September 14, 1998","origin":""}},"nopt":{"r":0},"desc":"friendly serial communication program","r":[["NAME","<p>xminicom - friendly serial communication program</p>"],["SYNOPSIS","<p><b>xminicom</b> <i>minicom-options</i></p>"],["DESCRIPTION","<p><b>Xminicom</b> is a script wrapper around <i>minicom.</i> It tries to find a color capable xterm or rxvt on your system, and then runs minicom with the -c (color) flag in a terminal session.</p>"],["OPTIONS","<p>See <i>minicom</i> (1).</p>"],["AUTHOR","<p>Miquel van Smoorenburg, miquels@cistron.nl</p>"],["SEE ALSO","<p>minicom(1)</p>"]]}